<section id="how-it-works" style="background:var(--paper-2); border-top:1px solid var(--hairline); border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline);">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="section-tag">How it works</div>
      <h2>Three stages, one continuous loop</h2>
      <p>Every cycle, the system reads all sensors, decides the current risk level, and drives the LEDs, exhaust fan relay, and OLED display accordingly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stages">
      <div class="stage s1">
        <span class="stage-tag">Stage 1</span>
        <h4>Safe</h4>
        <p>Default operating state — conditions are within normal range.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gas below 350 (analog units)</li>
          <li>Temperature below 35°C</li>
          <li>Green LED on, fan and relay off</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stage s2">
        <span class="stage-tag">Stage 2</span>
        <h4>Warning</h4>
        <p>Readings cross the first threshold — ventilation kicks in automatically.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gas 350–599, or temp 35–44.9°C</li>
          <li>Yellow LED on</li>
          <li>Relay + exhaust fan switched on</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stage s3">
        <span class="stage-tag">Stage 3</span>
        <h4>Danger</h4>
        <p>Critical hazard, fire detected, or SOS pressed — full alert.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gas ≥ 600, or temp ≥ 45°C</li>
          <li>Flame sensor triggered, or SOS pressed</li>
          <li>Red LED on, fan forced on, OLED shows EVACUATE</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

